From 96c786c59f4c2fadf02e7aa8580a2ebee6b662e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhuchen <zhuchen@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:51:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kebab: correct the cam_vdig comment

The comment claimed the stock overlay gives this rail as 1,100,000 uV.
That figure belongs to cam1 (qcom,cam-sensor@1: cam_vdig = pm8008_l1);
for the rear module the overlay points cam_vdig at pm8150a_s8 with
1,350,000 uV.  Record what the vendor actually does instead, and note
that mainline does not model that PMIC at all, so the property is only
there to give the driver an enable handle and the diagnostic has to say
what the rail really reads.
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts      | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
index d4b02f2bd..9ea6bea63 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
@@ -1566,11 +1566,20 @@ regulators {
 			pm8008_l1: ldo1 {
 				regulator-name = "pm8008_l1";
 				/*
-				 * cam_vdig. The vendor tree gives this rail as
-				 * a single point, rgltr-min == rgltr-max ==
-				 * 1100000 uV, not a range.
+				 * cam_vdig. Be aware this is NOT what the stock
+				 * overlay uses: for the rear module (qcom,cam-sensor@0)
+				 * it points cam_vdig at pm8150a_s8 with
+				 * rgltr-min == rgltr-max == 1350000 uV, and the
+				 * 1100000 uV / pm8008_l1 pairing belongs to cam1, a
+				 * different camera.  Mainline does not model that
+				 * PMIC, its SMPS8 rails are already on for other
+				 * consumers, and CAM_VDIG (tlmm 117) gates whichever
+				 * of them reaches the module, so this property is only
+				 * here to give the driver a supply it can enable.
+				 * What the rail actually reads is checked by the
+				 * diagnostic (regulators_after_power).
 				 *
-				 * 1100000 is NOT settable: the pm8008 LDO
+				 * 1104000 is NOT settable as 1100000: the pm8008 LDO
 				 * steps in 8 mV, so the core rounds min up to
 				 * 1104000 and max down to 1096000, gets
 				 * min > max and refuses:
-- 
